<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 41,710 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 41,710 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 41,710 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday, compared to 40,532 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Monday	    Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			25,480	    20,971</p>
<p>    Import cargo			16,230	    19,561</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight ships were expected to sail and 11 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Mogas		    25,000	 Athenian Success   23/5</p>
<p>Chemicals		 3,000	 Owl Trader	   26/5</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 50,000	 Al-Marwah	     due</p>
<p>Gas oil		  60,000	 CSP - 10	     27/5</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 30,000	 Ying Song Hu	 30/5</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	    7,000	 Patty Anne	   24/5</p>
<p>Vegoil		   18,000	 Ariston		27/5</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
